{"id": "EUVD-2024-55799", "enisaUuid": "c6b90df1-c6d6-32cc-98a7-85bc3908cd08", "description": "PhysicsFS through 3.2.0 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in __PHYSFS_utf8codepoint() that allows attackers to read past name buffers via an off-by-one cursor advance on six-octet UTF-8 sequences. Attackers can supply a crafted archive with entry names ending in six-octet sequences, causing PHYSFS_utf8stricmp() and hashing to over-read and crash the application.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T00:58:44", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/icculus/physfs/issues/79", "https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/physfs-utf8-decoder-overread", "https://github.com/icculus/physfs/blob/release-3.2.0/src/physfs_unicode.c#L165-L187", "https://github.com/icculus/physfs/commit/8a90802778f14dea9c086fb5436839181a3222d5", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/physicsfs-through-3.2.0-out-of-bounds-read-via-physfs-utf8codepoint"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f7r8-2vph-g5gv", "CVE-2024-58392"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "42eecbda-ad60-38d6-8590-cc6c48a55aef", "product": {"name": "PhysicsFS", "vendor": {"name": "icculus"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dfad1c00-05e5-3ac0-82a1-c8fbaf485b7b", "vendor": {"name": "icculus"}}], "isExploited": false}